# An EMITTED service is its own repository, and nothing above it ignores anything.
#
# Inside this monorepo `platform/.gitignore` covers these paths, so the
# absence of this file was invisible here -- and every service emitted by
# `scripts/new_service.sh` started DIRTY the first time anyone ran its tests.
# That is not cosmetic in this estate: the contract proof refuses a dirty tree,
# so a fresh service's own suite would refuse to run on a checkout whose only
# sin was having been run once. Measured 2026-09-05 on the three wave-1 repos:
# 17 untracked `__pycache__/` entries each, immediately after `pytest`.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Local virtualenvs and build output.
# The local knowledge graph. `graphify-repo-init.sh` writes graphify-out/ into
# whatever repository it is pointed at, and this estate's monorepo ignores it at
# the root -- so inside the monorepo a service submodule looked clean while its
# OWN rules said nothing, and one emitted service sat permanently
# untracked-dirty. An enclosing ignore rule is always a lie about the child: a
# submodule, and an emitted standalone service, inherit nothing.
graphify-out/

.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Terraform working state. `.terraform.lock.hcl` is TRACKED on purpose -- it is
# the supply-chain pin CI verifies against -- but the provider cache and any
# state or tfvars are not.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars

# Serverless Framework build output.
.serverless/
node_modules/

# The service's own local database, when it runs on the SQLite backend.
*.db
